# The sibling of string_field_default.z on the PARAMETER side. docs/spec.pdoc
# Restrictions: "A reftype value (heap-allocated string, list, map, user class)
# is not a valid default at this layer" -- a default is re-emitted verbatim and
# a String needs a runtime allocation.
#
# A field was refused here. A parameter was ACCEPTED, typed nothing, and said
# so only at the CALL -- `expected ?, got StringView` -- or, if nobody called
# it, `missing required arguments 'msg' (type: ?)` against the caller that
# never existed. Neither is the mistake, nor the place it was made.
opt: function {msg: "hi"} is {
    print msg
}

main: function is {
    opt msg: "there"
}
